{
 "sheet": 1,
 "name": "SN74CBT3253CPWR",
 "kind": "analog_switch",
 "manufacturer": "Texas Instruments",
 "title": "SN74CBT3253C: two 4-channel FET bus-switch multiplexers, 5 V, protected against undershoot to -2 V",
 "source": {
  "document": "SCDS123B",
  "revision": "July 2003, revised January 2007",
  "pages": 26
 },
 "summary": "Two 4-to-1 FET bus switches on a 4 V to 5.5 V supply. The select pair S0, S1 is shared by both multiplexers and each has its own active-low enable, 1OE and 2OE; a disabled multiplexer leaves its A port high-impedance from every B port. Signals pass in either direction through about 3 Ω, and a sensing circuit on the A and B ports keeps an off switch off while a port is pulled as far as -2 V. Ioff is specified, so the part isolates with VCC at 0. It comes in SOIC, SSOP, QSOP, TSSOP and VQFN; SN74CBT3253CPWR is the TSSOP-16 on a 2000-piece reel.",
